22. Shared Mailbox Permissions

A shared mailbox allows multiple authorized users to access a common mailbox.

Important permission concepts include:

Full Access

Allows an authorized user to access the mailbox.

Send As

Allows an authorized user to send an email that appears to come directly from the shared mailbox.

Example:

From: support@company.com
Send on Behalf

Allows an authorized user to send a message on behalf of the shared mailbox.

Example:

John on behalf of support@company.com
Help Desk example

User can open the shared mailbox but cannot send from it.

Investigate:

Send As / Send on Behalf permissions

